# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
# Libraries should not include pubspec.lock, per https://dart.dev/guides/libraries/private-files#pubspeclock.
/pubspec.lock
**/doc/api/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
/build/
/coverage/
examples

# The agent-instruction layer is shared with the team: CLAUDE.md, the
# AGENTS.md it imports, and the audit method those two point at.
#
# Working plans stay local. `/plans/*` rather than `/plans` is load-bearing:
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the two
# negations below only work when the directory itself stays un-ignored and its
# contents are excluded instead.
/plans/*
!/plans/AUDIT-METHOD.md
!/plans/check_citations.py
# Same shape as /plans above: the directory stays un-ignored so the
# negation can reach inside it. Agent guidance under doc/agents/ is
# shared; working plan drafts in doc/ stay local.
/doc/*
!/doc/agents/
!/doc/synced_sliver_tree_tutorial.md

# Claude Code's shared configuration is versioned: agents, skills, rules,
# workflows, hooks and settings. The agent worktrees are full
# checkouts of this repository, and settings.local.json holds one developer's
# own grants, so both stay local.
/.claude/worktrees/
/.claude/settings.local.json
